[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_7niso")
name = "Cataracts"
icon = ExtResource("1_bk1tu")
short_info = "CONTRAST RATIO 1.17:1"
manual_text = "[b][u]CLINICAL OVERVIEW[/u][/b]
A cataract is a condition in which the eye's lens becomes cloudy, significantly reducing vision quality and potentially leading to blindness. This opacification obstructs light from reaching the retina.  

[b][u]CAUSES AND RISKS[/u][/b]
[indent]
[b]•[/b] Commonly associated with aging, but can occur due to injuries, or diseases like glaucoma and diabetes.
[b]•[/b] Risk factors include steroid use, radiation exposure, smoking, and ultraviolet (UV) light.
[b]•[/b] It is a leading cause of blindness worldwide, although it is usually treatable through surgery.
[/indent] 
[b][u]VISUAL IMPACT[/u][/b]
This impairment manifests as a significant loss of contrast and a “foggy” or blurred overlay in the individual’s vision, making text nearly impossible to read when placed on similar-colored backgrounds."
related_wcag = ExtResource("1_f072e")
